    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0609" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365.115/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reed</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-15T19:00:00-05:00">November 15, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. Department has received copy of report without enclosures from the American
                    Consulate in Milan dated October 15, 1938 addressed to the Embassy<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d479-f1"/> concerning withdrawal of privileges at Milan Stock
                    Exchange from Robert Blattner, American citizen, as result of recent anti-Jewish
                    measures.</p>
                <p>Please report by cable whether the Embassy considers this discriminatory and if
                    so what action has been taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
